From b72f254b4e04f1b2282495fb2d5cd7e239c47d9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:54:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(sim): a stock-source chamfer's bevel is no credit
 over a part

The program sim credited the declared edge break (#303) of a 2D Chamfer
off the stock over every column under the stock's edge. A part added
after generation under that edge was thus judged as bevelled, the sim
found no gouge, the live re-judge of the kept parts (#1628) did not run,
and the chamfer's cut into the part posted.

The #1631 solid law forbids a stock-source chamfer to enter any part,
so the credit could only forgive a cut that the op law forbids. The sim
now credits no break of such an op (breaks_stock_edge in plan_program).
Where the sim finds a gouge, the gate also appends the kept_moved line,
so the refusal names the op and the part.

Pinned by tests/stock_chamfer_added_part.rs (aligned, quarter-turned
and hair-turned stock; a part clear of the cut still posts).

Fixes #2308

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
