From 820245b9b1ffc0653ce82200e58e22f93d736d0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:47:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(sim): a stock-source Deburr that cuts into a part
 never posts

A Deburr whose source is the setup's stock breaks the stock's edges.
It now takes the stock-source solid law against the setup's parts, and
the program sim gives its bevel no edge-break credit over a part's
columns, as for a stock-source 2D Chamfer (#2308). A part added after
generation is refused by name through the live re-judge.

A from-model stock whose facets equal a judged part in place is that
part: its Deburr keeps the credit, and that part is spared from the law.

Fixes #2313

